## 🧩 What I Learned

* The CLI is divided into different modes with different permissions
* The prompt (`>`, `#`, `(config)#`) tells you exactly where you are
* Commands only work in the correct mode
* The `?` command is extremely useful for discovering commands

## ⚠️ Challenges

* Initially tried running config commands in the wrong mode
* Had to pay attention to the prompt to understand where I was
* Some commands worked in one mode but failed in others, which helped clarify their purpose

## 🌍 Real-World Connection

This is similar to user roles in a system:

* User EXEC = basic user
* Privileged EXEC = admin viewing system
* Config mode = admin making changes

Understanding this is critical because misusing commands in production networks can lead to misconfigurations.

